  * Qt 6 — GNU LGPL v3 / GPL v3 / commercial (The Qt Company). Arora is
    a Qt application; qwebchannel.js used by the start page is served
    from Qt's own qrc:///qtwebchannel/ resource.
  * QtWebEngine — embeds Chromium/Blink (BSD-3-Clause) plus Chromium's
    many bundled third-party libraries (ICU, V8, ffmpeg snippets, zlib,
    NSS, etc.). The corresponding license texts ship with Qt's source
    and documentation packages (per-module LICENSE* files, reproducible
    from the installed qtattributionsscanner); `make bundle` ships this
    file plus LICENSE.GPL2/GPL3 in dist/ alongside the Qt libraries.
  * OpenSSL libcrypto — Apache License 2.0 (OpenSSL 3.x) / OpenSSL+SSLeay
    (1.x). src/securestore.cpp resolves EVP symbols at runtime via
    QLibrary for AES-256-GCM; Arora does not link or ship OpenSSL.

